# document_rhetoric.p0t — SC1: da clausole transienti a un Document IR.
#
# Tutti i contenuti sono fatti reali, non fixture da persistere:
# - Apollo 13: NASA, https://www.nasa.gov/missions/apollo/the-hard-won-triumph-of-the-apollo-13-mission-45-years-later/
# - subduzione: USGS, https://www.usgs.gov/special-topics/subduction-zone-science/science/introduction-subduction-zones-amazing-events
# - studi osservazionali: PubMed Central, https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10589119/
# - mercurio: Los Alamos National Laboratory, https://periodic.lanl.gov/80.shtml
#
# La lezione non nomina Document IR, archi, predicati o arita'. Una normale
# classe linguistica appresa parlando cambia la lettura dello stesso documento.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a taught rhetorical cue links stable document units]
!timeout 60
# BASELINE: le unita' e gli span sopravvivono, ma la cue non appartiene ancora
# a una classe retorica e quindi nessun arco viene inventato.
> read: Apollo 13 did not achieve its scientific goals. Notwithstanding, NASA's rescue mission was an agency triumph.
< Learned 0 fact(s), skipped 2.
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_0, 0)
!query document_unit(document_1, document_1_unit_1, 1)
!query document_unit_source(document_1_unit_0, "Apollo 13 did not achieve its scientific goals", range(0, 46))
!query document_unit_token_surface(document_1_unit_1, 1, notwithstanding)
!query! rhetorical_edge(document_1, document_1_unit_0, document_1_unit_1, contrast)

# LEZIONE NATURALE e REPLAY: la classe aperta e' gia' insegnabile; il nuovo
# consumer documentale la usa immediatamente senza ricompilare.
> "notwithstanding" is a contrastive connector.
< Learned: contrastive_connector(notwithstanding).
> Is notwithstanding a contrastive connector?
< Yes.
> read: Apollo 13 did not achieve its scientific goals. Notwithstanding, NASA's rescue mission was an agency triumph.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s) and 1 rhetorical relation(s)
!query rhetorical_edge(document_2, document_2_unit_0, document_2_unit_1, contrast)
!query current_document_relation(contrast)

[test transfer contrast composition and natural ablation]
!timeout 60
# TRANSFER@3: geologia, metodologia scientifica e chimica; l'ultimo caso
# compone l'arco con un fatto contenuto realmente estratto.
> read: Subduction zones occupy a small fraction of Earth's surface. Notwithstanding, they produce the world's largest earthquakes.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s) and 1 rhetorical relation(s)
!query current_document_relation(contrast)
> read: Observational studies can identify associations. Notwithstanding they cannot by themselves establish causality.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s) and 1 rhetorical relation(s)
!query current_document_relation(contrast)
> read: Mercury is a metal. Notwithstanding, mercury is liquid at ordinary temperatures.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s) and 1 rhetorical relation(s)
!query metal(mercury)
!query rhetorical_edge(document_5, document_5_unit_0, document_5_unit_1, contrast)

# CONTRAST PRECISION: una conseguenza non e' un contrasto; le unita' restano,
# ma la classe non autorizza l'arco sbagliato.
> read: Mercury has atomic number 80. Therefore, mercury is an element.
!query document_unit(document_6, document_6_unit_0, 0)
!query document_unit(document_6, document_6_unit_1, 1)
!query! current_document_relation(contrast)

# ABLATION PARLATA: rimuove la sola causa dell'arco anche dai documenti gia'
# osservati; unita', span e fatto sul mercurio restano vivi. In particolare non
# deve mai nascere il vecchio misclaim `contrastive_connector(forget)`.
> forget that notwithstanding is a contrastive connector
< I no longer treat «notwithstanding» as a contrastive connector.
!query! contrastive_connector(notwithstanding)
!query! contrastive_connector(forget)
!query! rhetorical_edge(document_5, document_5_unit_0, document_5_unit_1, contrast)
!query document_unit(document_5, document_5_unit_0, 0)
!query document_unit(document_5, document_5_unit_1, 1)
!query metal(mercury)
> read: Mercury is a metal. Notwithstanding, mercury is liquid at ordinary temperatures.
<! Mapped
!query! current_document_relation(contrast)

# RETEACH: lo stesso binario riacquista la capacita' e la usa su un nuovo
# documento vero.
> "notwithstanding" is a contrastive connector.
< Learned: contrastive_connector(notwithstanding).
> read: The platypus is a mammal. Notwithstanding, the platypus lays eggs.
<~ Mapped 2 document unit(s) and 1 rhetorical relation(s)
!query current_document_relation(contrast)
